      "rating_evidence": "Without video, threats and state changes are only known post-hoc through voice lines ('It shot a dart', 'You're opening it!'), with no distinct spatial or mechanical sound cues preceding them. Simultaneous voice lines at 12.1s and 20.5s directly mask competing instructions about threats and rules of engagement.",
      "uncertainties": [
        "0.0s: Opening phrase sounds like '...ipers in' or '...ivers in', cut off at start.",
        "12.0s: Calm voice says 'It shot an el...' before being interrupted.",
        "20.5s-25.8s: Lower voice says something like 'Scout the area... patrol... please annotate as hostile' underneath the high-pitched voice talking about unarmed ships not paying."
      ],
      "minimal_fix": "Implement a voice priority queue with ducking so the high-pitched announcer and secondary voices never speak simultaneously at 12.1s and 20.5s."
    },
    {
